  "final_answer_preview": "Section 45 of the Bharatiya Nyaya Sanhita, 2023 defines abetment as occurring when a person intentionally aids the doing of a thing through any act or illegal omission (Section 45(c)). Additionally, it includes engaging in conspiracy with others to commit that act, provided an act or illegal omission occurs in furtherance of that conspiracy (Section 45(b)). This section establishes the framework for understanding how abetment operates in relation to criminal acts.",
